  "term": "Pacinian corpuscle",
  "definition": "A Pacinian corpuscle is a touch receptor in the tissue under the skin, including both hairy and smooth skin. It contains a sensory nerve ending wrapped in many layered coverings and responds especially to rapid, high-frequency stimulation such as vibration over a relatively large area.",
